From 42bf90937029b07a3c928820b3c3ace3a53f921c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tedin7 <tommasoderosa94@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:35:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: rdna2spirv decodes scalar, image and buffer tuples
 that run into vcc from the blob when llvm-mc rejects them

llvm-mc skips the first word of s_buffer_load_dwordx8 into s[100:107], an image resource in s[100:107] or a buffer resource in s[104:107] and leaves the second word as junk, so translate() refused those shaders (reachable instruction with normalized encoding) or translated them without the load. restore_vcc_tuples reads the uncovered words of the code range with rdna2_decode and keeps only instructions whose operands hold a VCCTuple list, the form the translator already takes. Other undecodable words are unchanged.

